data: {"callId":"call-d1e3d80f-239e-428a-aadf-52bceefd4da9-2\nfc_454886fe-6798-9bce-bf65-ccb24a778db6_0","name":"get_mcp_tools","status":"completed","args":{"server":"cursor-cloud","toolName":"environment-info","toolCallId":"call-d1e3d80f-239e-428a-aadf-52bceefd4da9-2\nfc_454886fe-6798-9bce-bf65-ccb24a778db6_0"},"result":{"success":{"content":"{\n  \"tool\": \"environment-info\",\n  \"description\": \"Return the current cloud-agent run's environment (name, environment & version public ids, source, how/when it was recorded, repos, the full environment.json, a link to the environment in the cursor.com dashboard, and environmentDeleted when the linked environment is soft-deleted), a top-level `repos` array of canonical repository URLs (the same strings as `environment.repos` and the values `trigger-environment-build` `refs[].repoUrl` must match; still set when `environment` is null, from composer.repoUrl), the effective egress policy (allow-all, the complete merged allowed-domain list, or unresolved with a reason), the environment build the pod booted from (build id, snapshot id, git-setup mode, warm-fork mode); for a run that did not boot from a build, only the recorded resolution (no_finished_builds or no_healthy_builds), or null when none was recorded, and (for internal runs) the initiating Cursor client build info (version + commit SHA, same as Help → About). Use top-level `repos` when choosing `refs[].repoUrl`. Use `environmentJsonPath` to tell repo-file managed environments from db-backed ones: a present path (defaulting to `.cursor/environment.json`) means the config is read from that repository environment.json (repo-file managed), while a null/absent path means a db-backed snapshot config (db-managed). When environmentDeleted is true, treat the environment as historical only — do not trigger new builds or treat the environment id as live.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {},\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"\n  }\n}"}}}

