data: {"callId":"call-d1e3d80f-239e-428a-aadf-52bceefd4da9-7\nfc_454886fe-6798-9bce-bf65-ccb24a778db6_5","name":"grep_search","status":"completed","args":{"pattern":"rustup|cargo install|prerequisites|getting started|dev environment","path":"/workspace/docs","glob":"*.md","caseInsensitive":false,"headLimit":40,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-d1e3d80f-239e-428a-aadf-52bceefd4da9-7\nfc_454886fe-6798-9bce-bf65-ccb24a778db6_5","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"rustup|cargo install|prerequisites|getting started|dev environment","path":"/workspace/docs","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/workspace":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"docs/verse/tutorial-quests.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":50,"content":"- Microcoder: `cargo install --path crates/microcoder --locked` from a"}]},{"file":"docs/verse/first-agent-quests.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":26,"content":"references and missing prerequisites. Task completion, activity, and disappearing"}]},{"file":"docs/verse/engine/architecture.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":339,"content":"streaming are subsequent work rather than prerequisites for the first original"}]},{"file":"docs/verse/blender-pipeline.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":354,"content":"  `oxipng` (`cargo install oxipng`), keeping its 8-bit color type, and"}]},{"file":"docs/verse/agent-trainer-leveling.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":544,"content":"### Phase 4: Purses, if the prerequisites hold"},{"lineNumber":583,"content":"  prerequisites hold. Otherwise XP becomes a currency and farming pays."}]},{"file":"docs/verification.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":83,"content":"prerequisites the later phases assume: a file-descriptor limit of at least"},{"lineNumber":85,"content":"the soft limit itself), `cargo`, `python3`, `git`, and `rustup` on PATH, and"}]},{"file":"docs/transcripts/README.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":83,"content":"| [241](241.md)–[247](247.md) | Khala orchestration, OpenCode/Codex integration, Khala Code, dogfooding, and selling. | Tests orchestration in real tools and discovers that capacity, continuity, and dependable UX are prerequisites for the market story. |"}]},{"file":"docs/transcripts/243.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":206,"content":"Did this finish? Thank God. Okay. \"Deploy landed. Running the live monotonicity...\" Okay, please refresh and then work. Okay, 11.2. No, I still see it. \"Sometimes a sub-agent will do a push that doesn't have the latest changes. Rebased, so at least this should be working.\" Correct the \"big pickle, the big pickle\" — you gotta get your Big Pickle straight, people. Well, this is — yeah, I don't care. I don't care. Okay. OpenCode can do meaningful work for us. Good. Good. 12.3. \"Let me diagnose fast: is the deployed client overcounting, or is your browser serving a stale cache bundle?\" No. All our sub-agents are finishing. I can't believe it. 12 million tokens. 12 million tokens. We're just getting started, people. We're just getting started."}]},{"file":"docs/transcripts/138.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":13,"content":"**[00:00] Speaker:** Hard to believe we're celebrating one year of this series. Year one, first of many. We're at 137 episodes, and you know, you might think that's a lot, but we're trying to catch up to Handmade Hero here, this project from Casey. You know, they got they got they got they got 667 episodes. So we're just we're just getting started here at Open Agents. But I wanted to review what we did for the last year for those just tuning in or curious what we've been up to. And let's start by asking Open Agents what we've been up to. So scrape the video series link and summarize the topics here in two paragraphs. This is our pro interface. We're gonna start opening this up to the public quite soon. But yeah, our video series so far has documented the development of an open source AI agents platform, spanning 137 episodes from initial setup to advanced features. The early episodes cover foundational work, including tech stack selection, Laravel implementation, and basic agent princi [... omitted end of long line]"}]},{"file":"docs/transcripts/126.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":13,"content":"**[00:00] Speaker:** Well, folks, I asked our agents, and they said that they're bored and looking for work. So, you know, we watched this video about WordPress running 43% of all sites on the internet, apparently. And it turns out that WordPress is basically run by one maniacal, extortionate, villainous thug, Matt Mullenweg. Holy shit. So unbelievable. So Theo had a video called This Might Be the End of WordPress last week. That was pretty good. He then interviewed Mullenweg. I listened to that. I was like, well, Mullenweg's clearly the villain here. And then this WP engine. Great company, from what I could tell. I used them happily 10 years ago. They're also here in Austin. I see their, you know, big ass building downtown. Really successful company building on WordPress. You know, as the founder of WordPress, you'd think you'd be happy about that. But, ooh, you're using our, you're using WP and my mom got confused. Like Mullenweg, what a fucking idiot. OK, so I don't really care. I'm [... omitted end of long line]"}]},{"file":"docs/terminal/issue-roadmap.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":82,"content":"The following tables record the initial scope and native prerequisites."}]},{"file":"docs/terminal/scope.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":371,"content":"3. **From source:** `cargo install --path crates/openagents-cli` plus"}]},{"file":"docs/sales/revenue-roadmap.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":240,"content":"| World prerequisites | Closed [#10786](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10786), [#10789](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10789); open [#10788](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10788), [#10790](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10790), [#10791](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10791); [generative agents](../verse/generative-agents.md#phases-and-dependencies) | Reuse the landed town clock and checked-citation reflection; finish the existing world-tree, day-plan, and roster issues without duplicate foundations |"}]},{"file":"docs/sales/agent-sales-floor.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":917,"content":"and migration are not prerequisites for local Paul preparation. Enable each"}]},{"file":"docs/release/terminal.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":75,"content":"`rustup target add <target>` inside the checkout, so the pinned toolchain"}]},{"file":"docs/sales/README.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":574,"content":"organizes all filed work and shared prerequisites by delivery, workstream,"}]},{"file":"docs/research/unreal/nanite.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":309,"content":"The Nanite feature entry still describes older Windows graphics prerequisites. The broader **UE 5.8 engine/editor minimum** is newer: Windows 10 22H2, or Enterprise 21H2; Windows 11 is recommended. Feature-level API prerequisites and current engine support policy are not the same thing. [Epic Games Developers](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine/hardware-and-software-specifications-for-unreal-engine)"}]},{"file":"docs/roadmap/2026-09-28-tassadar-revival.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":363,"content":"Rust only once the current prerequisites hold:"}]},{"file":"docs/roadmap.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":302,"content":"| Nostr markets and earlier swap infrastructure | Reuse bilateral negotiation, provider independence, exact obligations, and recovery. Swaps, liquidity markets, and financial risk products are not prerequisites for Coder or labor. |"}]},{"file":"docs/protocol/2026-09-26-nip-implementation-coverage.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":45,"content":"checks, omitted prerequisites, and deployment verification. This change does"},{"lineNumber":190,"content":"  commands, feature scope, failures, and omitted prerequisites. Production"}]},{"file":"docs/protocol/2026-09-26-upstream-nip-sync-block.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":154,"content":"6. FI deployment as a separately scoped project with JWT/JWKS, all ingress paths, session/disconnect races and privacy tests. PMA remains rejected until its complete staged migration prerequisites exist."}]},{"file":"docs/protocol/implementation-plan.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":54,"content":"prerequisites are proven. FI and the public Buzz push gateway do not block"}]},{"file":"docs/protocol/2026-09-26-upstream-nip-sync.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":51,"content":"| First | Block PMA, kind 30179 | New draft explicitly requires rejection until its privacy, CAS, recovery, and revocation gates exist. Generic admission currently has no such rejection or private-read rule. | Reject public writes; audit import/restore and stored-record visibility. Keep PMA unadvertised and inert until its complete migration prerequisites exist. |"},{"lineNumber":134,"content":"   consumer, exact scope, and fixtures. Follow PMA's staged prerequisites before"}]},{"file":"docs/protocol/2026-09-26-teardown-coverage.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":156,"content":"| [linear-agents.md](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/blob/8f84d05896ef14edee491621bf977ee5315cc8ed/docs/teardowns/linear-agents.md) (§§3,8,11,18;120–152,340–401,452–491,658–739) | Human accountability plus bounded agent delegate; typed visible activities; durable questions; narrow useful task classes; review cost and accepted outcomes; organization guidance. | POL grant/instruction boundaries; CTX frame; CJ/RUN; LAB verification/acceptance. | WORK durable objective and planning; SESS activity/question; AUTO loops; WS context resources. Vendor preview expectations and timing goals are historical evidence, not normative OpenAgents constants. “First pass every bug” failed; task specificity and verification are prerequisites, not universal completion claims. |"}]},{"file":"docs/protocol/verification/2026-09-26-nips/README.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":72,"content":"See the [verification policy](../../../verification.md) for prerequisites and"},{"lineNumber":140,"content":"external prerequisites cannot establish those behaviors."}]},{"file":"docs/project-board.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":132,"content":"| Dependencies | All native prerequisites, including completed foundations |"}]},{"file":"docs/maintenance/2026-09-26-documentation-review.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":40,"content":"| Deployment | Update migration/configuration references and Debian commands. Remove rollback advice that could erase migration-ledger history. Distinguish operator prerequisites from completed release evidence. |"}]},{"file":"docs/minecraft/delivery-and-sources.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":29,"content":"| [Runs #9510](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/9510), [children #9511](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/9511), [packages #9512](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/9512), [evidence #9513](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/9513) | Shared runtime prerequisites have partial implementations and outstanding acceptance work |"},{"lineNumber":59,"content":"| MC-04 | Shared claims and compute accounting | Atomic local claims/holds, provider handoff reconciliation, no duplicate dispatch or overspend | MC-02; COORD/POL/RUN prerequisites |"}]},{"file":"docs/laya/README.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":128,"content":"- [`../decision-models/others/laya-adapter-prerequisites.md`](../decision-models/others/laya-adapter-prerequisites.md)"},{"lineNumber":129,"content":"  — licenses, artifact sources, deployment prerequisites, and the"}]},{"file":"docs/lev/helper-build.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":12,"content":"Running the helper also requires the Apple Intelligence prerequisites described"}]},{"file":"docs/kev/2026-09-20-upstream-review.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":202,"content":"program-selection suite are prerequisites for the new 4B evaluation."}]},{"file":"docs/history/2026-09-25-transcript-roadmap.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":23,"content":"are not prerequisites. The [networked Coder plan](../coder/design/networked-coder-plan.md)"}]},{"file":"docs/game/playtesting.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":910,"content":"  [prerequisites](../verse/agent-trainer-leveling.md#rewards), and"}]}],"totalLines":106,"totalMatchedLines":106,"clientTruncated":true,"headLimitApplied":40}}}}}}

