rom composer.repoUrl), the effective egress policy (allow-all, the complete merged allowed-domain list, or unresolved with a reason), the environment build the pod booted from (build id, snapshot id, git-setup mode, warm-fork mode); for a run that did not boot from a build, only the recorded resolution (no_finished_builds or no_healthy_builds), or null when none was recorded, and (for internal runs) the initiating Cursor client build info (version + commit SHA, same as Help → About). Use top-level `repos` when choosing `refs[].repoUrl`. Use `environmentJsonPath` to tell repo-file managed environments from db-backed ones: a present path (defaulting to `.cursor/environment.json`) means the config is read from that repository environment.json (repo-file managed), while a null/absent path means a db-backed snapshot config (db-managed). When environmentDeleted is true, treat the environment as historical only — do not trigger new builds or treat the environment id as live.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {},\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\"\n  }\n}"}}},"toolCallId":"call-5b2a3556-4624-49e5-a4f6-67eaff67afa7-3\nfc_3aea6d02-b52f-9613-896d-e71fd9f5e1bb_0","startedAtMs":"1791473824859","completedAtMs":"1791473825067"}},{"toolCall":{"shellToolCall":{"args":{"command":"cargo fetch --locked --offline; echo \"FETCH_EXIT:$?\"","workingDirectory":"/workspace","timeout":600000,"toolCallId":"call-5b2a3556-4624-49e5-a4f6-67eaff67afa7-4\nfc_3aea6d02-b52f-9613-896d-e71fd9f5e1bb_1","simpleCommands":["cargo","echo"],"parsingResult":{"executableCommands":[{"name":"cargo","args":[{"type":"word","value":"fetch"},{"type":"word","value":"--locked"},{"type":"word","value":"--offline"}],"fullText":"cargo fetch --locked --offline"},{"name":"echo","args":[{"type":"string","value":"\"FETCH_EXIT:$?\""}],"fullText":"echo \"FETCH_EXIT:$?\""}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","timeoutBehavior